# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.meta

# ...except .meta for source we actually track. The committed scenes reference
# these scripts by GUID (MainWorld.unity alone holds ~29k such references), and
# the GUID lives only in the .meta. Without them a restore from this repo gives
# you the scenes and the scripts but no way to reconnect them - every component
# comes back as "missing script". ~890 files, ~197 KB.
# Deliberately NOT un-ignoring .meta for untracked third-party/art assets.
!Assets/Scripts/**/*.cs.meta
!Assets/Scripts/**/*.asmdef.meta

# The same for the UI Toolkit screens, styles and panel settings: scenes reference the UXML
# documents and panel settings by GUID, so without these a restore leaves every HUD document empty.
!Assets/UI/**/*.meta
!Assets/UI/**/*.asset

# Building definitions (TownHouse assets). The village references them by GUID, and the type each
# one carries decides which skill a house boosts, so they must be versioned with their metas.
!Assets/Prefabs/Buildings/*.asset
!Assets/Prefabs/Buildings/*.asset.meta

# The embedded Unity Toon Shader package (patched for URP in Unity 6.7). Materials reference its shaders by the
# GUIDs the registry package has, which live in these metas.
!Packages/com.unity.toonshader/**/*.meta

# The home island terrain, versioned through LFS (see .gitattributes) now that build mode reshapes
# it. The two other terrain tiles are much larger and stay out until LFS quota is decided.
!Assets/New Terrain.asset
!Assets/New Terrain.asset.meta

# Our own village models, built from code by tools/village-rebuild/blender, and their materials. The scenes
# reference them by GUID, so the metas are versioned too. Derived/ holds edited copies of kit meshes, which
# stay out like the kits themselves.
!Assets/Village.meta
!Assets/Village/**
Assets/Village/Derived/
Assets/Village/Derived.meta

# World resource types (trees, gather spots). Fields in the scenes reference them by GUID. The meshes they
# draw are baked from kit models into WorldResources/Models and stay out like the kits; rebuild them with
# Ravenfall > World Resources > Create Type From Selection.
!Assets/World.meta
!Assets/World/WorldResources.meta
!Assets/World/WorldResources/Types.meta
!Assets/World/WorldResources/Types/*.asset
!Assets/World/WorldResources/Types/*.asset.meta

# Grass: the shader, its materials and the profile, all ours. The blades are generated in code.
!Assets/World/Grass.meta
!Assets/World/Grass/**

# Our post effects (tilt shift), loaded from their Resources folder.
!Assets/World/PostEffects.meta
!Assets/World/PostEffects/**

# The sea (its shader is referenced by the scene's Ocean) and the sky's clouds (loaded from Resources).
!Assets/World/Water.meta
!Assets/World/Water/**
!Assets/World/Sky.meta
!Assets/World/Sky/**
# The islands' ground shader and its material (the terrain references the material by GUID).
!Assets/World/Terrain.meta
!Assets/World/Terrain/**
# The weather and ambient particles' shader, loaded from Resources.
!Assets/World/Ambience.meta
!Assets/World/Ambience/**
# The swaying plants' shader, loaded from Resources.
!Assets/World/Foliage.meta
!Assets/World/Foliage/**
# The own boats' prefabs (docs/own-boats.md), made from the kits by tools/sailing/make-boat-prefabs.cs and
# referenced by the scene's OwnBoatPrefabs.
!Assets/World/Sailing.meta
!Assets/World/Sailing/**
# The quest marks over NPCs' heads (IslandNpc), drawn with the Image Generator, loaded from Resources.
!Assets/World/Markers.meta
!Assets/World/Markers/**
# Hero mode's skill icons and HUD art (HeroHudView, HeroMinimap), drawn with the Image Generator, loaded from Resources.
!Assets/World/Hero.meta
!Assets/World/Hero/**
# Ironhill's own pieces (the sleeping dragon's animator), docs/ironhill-rework.md
!Assets/World/Ironhill.meta
!Assets/World/Ironhill/**

# Local safety copies made before reshaping terrain or scenes.
Backups/

# Unity3D Generated File On Crash Reports
sysinfo.txt

# Builds
*.apk
*.unitypackage

# Font Awesome 7 metadata (icons.json and friends), local reference only: over 150 MB
tools/fontawesome7-metadata/

# The Image Generator's worker: built on first use by the editor (ImageGen.cs).
tools/ImageGenService/bin/
tools/ImageGenService/obj/
!tools/ImageGenService/ImageGenService.csproj
